# Shell scripts need real LF line endings regardless of a checkout's
# core.autocrlf - a CRLF-mangled shebang line breaks execution outright,
# and mid-script \r characters can silently corrupt string comparisons
# even when the script still runs. Without this, Windows clones with
# core.autocrlf=true would check these out as CRLF and break the
# pre-commit hooks that shell out to them
# (dbt_football_snowflake/.hooks/*.sh).
*.sh text eol=lf
